@startuml seq_assign_developer
title Sequence — Assign a Developer (permission AND scope)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam actorBorderColor #808080
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBorderColor #808080
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam databaseBorderColor #808080
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #808080
skinparam sequenceReferenceBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #808080
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
autonumber

actor "Director / Project Manager" as U
participant "Frontend" as SPA
participant "TeamController" as TC
participant "ProjectScopeService" as SCOPE
participant "TeamService" as TS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

U -> SPA : choose a developer
SPA -> TC : POST /api/projects/{id}/team
TC -> TC : permission ASSIGN_DEVELOPER\n(@PreAuthorize)
TC -> SCOPE : is the project within\nthe caller's scope?
SCOPE -> DB : accessible projects (1 EXISTS query)

alt out of scope or missing permission
  TC --> SPA : 403 Forbidden
else authorized
  TC -> TS : assign(projectId, userId, roleInTeam)
  TS -> DB : INSERT team_assignments
  TC --> SPA : 201 Created
end

note over TC, SCOPE
  Two distinct checks: permission, then project scope.
end note

@enduml
